* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_ptdf (reference/crafted.toml, 17 Nov 2026): demo12_pfd (the
* power-flow grid of nodes ELC in REG1 and REG2 and TRAELC in REG1, with the allocation of
* generation and demand to grid nodes) in the PTDF formulation (powerflo.vda L43-44, L59-64,
* L70, L86, L98-99, L172-178, L229-249, L262-287; M1.3 change 57), which no open model reaches:
* - PTDF factors for the REG1-REG2 line and for the line from ELC to TRAELC in REG1. Those of
*   REG2's end of the REG1-REG2 line are cleared (L174); one factor falls below the tolerance
*   1E-5 from 2030 (L175); those of the TRAELC end are made the opposite of the ELC end's (L59-64);
* - the REG1-REG2 line, with no past capacity, is a candidate line: CAP_BND UP in 2010 and 2030
*   gives its virtual capacity GR_CAPUP (L238-239), and the rows EQ_GR_VIRTCAP and EQ_GR_VIRTBND;
* - the ELC-TRAELC line has a past investment (NCAP_PASTI 2000): no new capacity (L177), and it
*   stops being a candidate while its past capacity lasts (L234-235).
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
PARAMETER GR_PTDF /
REG1.2005.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.ELC.REG1.ELC 0.3
REG1.2005.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.ELC.REG2.ELC -0.7
REG1.2030.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.ELC.REG2.ELC 4E-6
REG2.2005.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.ELC.REG1.ELC 0.5
REG1.2005.TU_ELC_TRA1.ELC.REG1.ELC 0.6
REG1.2005.TU_ELC_TRA1.ELC.REG2.ELC 0.2
REG1.2005.TU_ELC_TRA1.TRAELC.REG1.ELC -0.4
/;

PARAMETER CAP_BND /
REG1.2010.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.UP 5
REG1.2030.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.UP 8
/;

PARAMETER NCAP_PASTI /
REG1.2000.TU_ELC_TRA1 3
/;
